# Trivy ignore list for the backend image scan (.github/workflows/trivy-scan.yml).
#
# Every entry needs: why it isn't exploitable here, what would let us drop it,
# and an `exp:` date so it stops suppressing the finding automatically and has
# to be re-justified.

# CVE-2026-47884 — spring-webmvc 6.2.19 (from Spring Boot 3.5.16): RCE via
# improper path limitation in XsltView. Not reachable: the app configures no
# XSLT views (no XsltView / XsltViewResolver anywhere in core or addons), and
# its REST controllers render JSON/CSV/PDF, not server-side views. The only
# fixed release is Spring Framework 7.0.9 (Spring Boot 4, a major upgrade); no
# 6.2.x fix exists yet. Drop this entry when a 6.2.x patch ships (bump via the
# Spring Boot BOM or a spring-framework.version override) or on moving to Boot 4.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-01-06
